### 3.1 Initialize Git Repository
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "chore: initial project scaffold"
```

### 3.2 Create GitHub Repository
1. Go to **github.com → New repository**
2. Name it `cicd-quality-demo`
3. Keep it **public** (Actions free tier is generous for public repos)
4. Do NOT initialize with README (we already have one)

### 3.3 Push Local Code
```bash
git remote add origin https://github.com/<YOUR_USERNAME>/cicd-quality-demo.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

### 3.4 Branch Strategy (Learn PR-based flow)
```
main          ← protected, only merged via PR
  └── feature/add-multiply   ← create PRs from here
```

```bash
git checkout -b feature/add-multiply
# make changes
git push origin feature/add-multiply
# open PR on GitHub → watch Actions run!
```

